how is the floppy pen when you wiggle it loosely in between your fingers and a toy bow with a suction cup with a string thats not wound tight and the grip of the pen by the hand related
\par 09:31
\par These three phenomena are related through }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid14158252\charrsid14158252 standing wave mechanics}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14158252\charrsid14158252 , }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\insrsid14158252\charrsid14158252 node/antinode physics}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14158252\charrsid14158252 , and }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid14158252\charrsid14158252 rotational pivots}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14158252\charrsid14158252 .
\par Here is exactly how these three specific examples connect:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid14158252\charrsid14158252 1. The Floppy Pen Illusion
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14158252\charrsid14158252 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar
