\insrsid14158252\charrsid14158252 
. Your peripheral vision has low visual acuity and is highly sensitive to motion, not fine detail. If a small patch of photoreceptors stops firing (a dead pixel), your brain doesn't see a black spot. Instead, it simply lacks data from that specific zone.

